# kernel q89y (TRIAL) = q89x - 0001-infiniti 0132 (one cluster power domain for all 8 CPUs, the upstream / SuperTurtleDev topology), 7.3.0-rc7-iceland-00530-g242d83c86fe0:
# q90c (TRIAL, 21 Oct 2026) = q90b + 0005-q90c: the display clock controller's own MX vote (dt-bindings + kaanapali.dtsi;
# docs/DISPLAY-CX-VOTE-FIX-2026-10-21.md). No C change: q90b's Image and modules, new device trees only.
# q90d (TRIAL, 22 Oct 2026) = q90c + 0006-q90d: dwc3-qcom keeps the interconnect votes across runtime suspend on
# Kaanapali (the display glitch fix; dwc3_qcom.keep_icc_runtime=0 = upstream), serial: qcom-geni: Clear pending IRQs
# while suspended (pw 1190182). docs/DISPLAY-CX-VOTE-FIX-2026-10-21.md.
# q90e (TRIAL, 22 Oct 2026) = q90d + 0007-q90e: drm/msm/a8xx crash state capture opt-in (msm.a8xx_crashstate, default
# off): the capture's GMU CX register read raised a synchronous external abort and GPU recovery never ran.
# q90f (TRIAL, 22 Oct 2026) = q90e + 0008-q90f: A840 Kaanapali protect table (msm.a8xx_legacy_protect), no submit
# replay on a GPU that was not reset (msm.a8xx_safe_recover).
# q90g (TRIAL, 22 Oct 2026) = q90f + 0009-q90g: idle refresh round (input activity filter,
# msm.dpu_idle_rr_qos_release: relax the 0335 latency request at the idle rate, default off).
# q90h (TRIAL, 22 Oct 2026) = q90g + 0010-q90h: qcom_battmgr OPLUS power_now at the nominal voltage of
# energy_now (qcom_battmgr.oplus_power_nominal, default Y), so that energy_now / power_now = charge_now / current_now.
# q90i (TRIAL, 22 Oct 2026) = q90h + 0011-q90i: memlat devfreq read-back polling off by default (B1), and
# configs/q90i.config (VA_BITS 48, HZ 250, PREEMPT_DYNAMIC with full preemption by default, ATH12K_DEBUG /
# CoreSight / STM off; config only, no tree change).
# q90j (TRIAL, 22 Oct 2026) = q90i without its six diagnostics-only patches: 0002-iceland 0353 (smp2p_sleepstate
# A/B switches), 0003-glitchfix 0003 / 0004 (GLITCH-DIAG debugfs files), 0006-q90d rpmhpd.kaanapali_mmcx_cx_parent,
# 0008-q90f msm.dpu_intf_diag, 0009-q90g raise_commit counters. Every TREE_AFTER from 0002 on is q90j's
# (0006 / 0008 / 0009 re-exported); the config is q90i's. Kernel 7.3.0-next-20261020-iceland-00457-g8c8519cc8363.
# q90k (TRIAL, 23 Oct 2026) = q90j + 0012-q90k: ath12k station power save in vif_cfg_changed (kernel-topics
# 5838d806db9d; upstream had it and reverted it for WCN7850 throughput), PSCI SYSTEM_RESET2 vendor resets as
# reboot-mode (kernel-topics tech/pm/power) + nvmem-reboot-mode cell length fix + psci.vendor_reset switch +
# the iceland /psci/reboot-mode bootloader node, qcom-cci reset on runtime resume (pw 1189997), DPU single flush
# of a shared video CTL (msm.dpu_dual_dsi_single_flush, default off), A840 KGSL workaround values
# (msm.a8xx_kgsl_eco, default off; with it KGSL's whole A840 table), GMU BCL (msm.a8xx_kgsl_bcl, default
# off), GPU_CLX_EN_REQ in the TZ request (msm.a8xx_clx_tz_flag, default off, only with msm.enable_clx=1),
# iris: EOS only for the drain LAST buffer (seek fix for FFmpeg v4l2m2m). Config = q90j's.
# Kernel 7.3.0-next-20261020-iceland-00474-g9bd5b02f1103.
# q90l (TRIAL, 23 Oct 2026) = q90k + 0013-q90l: ath12k no 'sband is NULL' warning when the RX channel fallback
# is the expected one (invalid PHY-metadata channel number, centre frequency within 160 MHz of the RX channel;
# dev_dbg_ratelimited instead). Config = q90k's. Kernel 7.3.0-next-20261020-iceland-00475-g80df3fcf6e51.
# q90m (TRIAL, 24 Oct 2026) = q90l + 0014-q90m: the Gunyah host stack as in-tree modules (android17-6.18 import,
# adapted to 7.3, unload, vCPU status, GuestAccept; configs/q90m.config: CONFIG_GUNYAH and friends =m, nothing loads at
# boot), msm.a8xx_clx_tz_flag default Y and the C binder + binderfs (revert of its removal). Kernel 7.3.0-next-20261020-iceland-00485-g317e59a58503.
# q90n (TRIAL, 24 Oct 2026) = q90m + 0015-q90n: qmp-combo DP-only PCS + UFS ESI after reset (pw 1191470 /
# 1191467), iris 64 capture buffers + VSP clock for high bitrates, lpass rx/tx/va/wsa macro clocks under runtime PM,
# the PMIC BCL hwmon driver + pmih0108 node (probes only with qcom_bcl_hwmon.enable=1), gunyah_timer.ko; configs/q90n.config:
# ANON_VMA_NAME, soft + buddy hard-lockup detectors, ARM64_PSEUDO_NMI (off until irqchip.gicv3_pseudo_nmi=1), BCL =m.
# Kernel 7.3.0-next-20261020-iceland-00497-gd0cd8dc8fa4d.
# q90o (TRIAL, 24 Oct 2026) = q90n + 0016-q90o: the q90n BCL hwmon driver, its pmih0108 node and switch
# reverted (the built-in thermal qcom-spmi-bcl already binds the bcl@4700 nodes), gunyah rsc_mgr unregisters its PM
# notifier on unload (suspend oops after modprobe -r). configs/q90o.config: no symbol (BCL gone with the driver).
# Kernel 7.3.0-next-20261020-iceland-00501-g93375214c848.
# q90p (TRIAL, 24 Oct 2026) = q90o + 0017-q90p: the iceland built-in defaults of the msm / panel
# switches (CONFIG_DRM_MSM_ICELAND_DEFAULTS; preemption / CLX only with the vendor533 GPU pair), a
# configurable default cpuidle governor, a build-time s2idle default. configs/q90p.config: those +
# RCU_NOCB_CPU_DEFAULT_ALL, lazy RCU on by default. Kernel 7.3.0-next-20261020-iceland-00505-gd18e14392cfc.
# q90q (TRIAL, 24 Oct 2026) = q90p + 0018-q90q: gunyah vm_mgr no WARN on unload, qmp-combo / qmp-usb system
# PM callbacks, remoteproc pas DTB release, geni AUTOCTS, dwc3-qcom hcd check, ucsi_glink no suspend in a
# notification, arm-smmu-qcom suspended fault-info, fastrpc duplicate maps, cpucp readq, q6apm guard.
# configs/q90q.config: no symbol. Kernel 7.3.0-next-20261020-iceland-00516-g1d3dd350d42e.
# q90r (TRIAL, 24 Oct 2026) = q90q + 0019-q90r: drm/msm Assorted fixes Oct 1-6 (pw 1192617), qrtr re-announce
# (1191447), mac80211 MLO multicast dedup (1192424) + TX_CTL_AMPDU (1192062), qmp-combo DP-only v1 reverted + v2
# (1192123), ufs core link recovery (1192082). configs/q90r.config: no symbol. Kernel 7.3.0-next-20261020-iceland-00529-gb04181fcf88f.
# q90s4 (25 Oct 2026) = q90r + 0020-q90s: 0001 the gunyah-cma-mem binding made valid YAML / schema;
# 0002 ucsi_glink: notifications quiesced across system sleep; 0003 ath12k: opt-in cold boot calibration
# (ath12k.cold_boot_cal, default off); 0004 iris: opt-in decode-order output (qcom_iris.decode_order_output,
# default off); 0005 gunyah: no release of still-donated / assigned memory; 0006 gunyah_qcom: failed demand-page
# assign logging (debug_assign, default off). configs/q90s.config: CONFIG_VHOST_NET=m. Kernel 7.3.0-next-20261020-iceland-00535-ge0ecda4a8eb6.
# q90t (25 Oct 2026) = q90s4 + 0021-q90t: UFS device-management timeouts in jiffies + runtime
# resume errors propagated (pw 1192856 1/2/3/5), ICE enable order + runtime PM (pw 1191193 2/3, 3/3) and
# optional tunables, all off by default: ICE power/control (auto), scmi_qcom_memlat_devfreq.stock_gating,
# panel_novatek_nt36536.cabc_mode, ath12k.pcie_ltr_off, spi_geni_qcom.gpi_cpu_latency_us.
# configs/q90t.config: BLK_WBT (not on by default), ZRAM_BACKEND_LZ4. Kernel 7.3.0-next-20261020-iceland-00546-gd4ae0205473d.
# q90u (26 Oct 2026) = q90t + 0022-q90u: ath12k creates its device debugfs files once with their
# directory; gunyah reports a missing resource manager log at info level. Every tunable stays at its
# default (off). Kernel 7.3.0-next-20261020-iceland-00548-g18ffc096fcee.
# q90v (26 Oct 2026) = q90u + 0023-q90v: gunyah refuses a protected VM whose shared guest memory
# is private anonymous memory (clear message at VM start instead of an endless fault loop) and
# keeps the start error. Every tunable stays at its default (off). Kernel 7.3.0-next-20261020-iceland-00549-g9bf8752f1b8a.
# q90w2 (26 Oct 2026) = q90v + 0024-q90w2: dwc3 resume-hs-terminations on Kaanapali (Peter Chen's
# patch), the wcd939x-usbss MG2_MISC address, wcd-clsh-v2 force IQ only without flyback users,
# the wcd939x version read after the TX device attached, and the v1.1+ bandgap fine adjust.
# Every tunable stays at its default (off). Kernel 7.3.0-next-20261020-iceland-00554-g87174e7e291d.
# q90x (27 Oct 2026) = q90w2 + 0025-q90x: ktz8869_iceland starts at stock's default brightness
# (1417 of 4095) instead of 2047. Config and device tree as q90w2. Kernel 7.3.0-next-20261020-iceland-00555-gbc55efdfac46.
# q90y (28 Oct 2026) = q90x + 0026-q90y: Perpetua review picks - qrtr ns keeps announcing after a failed
# send (Igor Opaniuk), dwc3-qcom VBUS override for the role entered, the battmgr charge current cooling
# device and the weighted thermal sensor (neither used by the device tree). Config: + configs/q90y.config.
# Kernel 7.3.0-next-20261020-iceland-00561-g94aa2d05027c.
# q90z (30 Oct 2026) = q90y + 0027-q90z: bwmon zone1 3, iris NoC LPI poll, ICE OPP clock scaling with UFS +
# the kaanapali ICE OPP table, qrtr re-announce v3 (replaces v1), dwc3 UTMI pipe clock in DP-only modes,
# L2F always on. Config: + configs/q90z.config (SWIOTLB 2 MB dynamic, CMA 128 MB).
# Kernel 7.3.0-next-20261020-iceland-00572-ga7adbdc40113.
# q91c (2 Nov 2026): the queue re-based onto v7.4-rc1 (6628e7d4c6b2). Every series 0001-0027 is regenerated
# from its rc1 replay (same file names); 12 patches merged upstream by rc1 are gone (numbers kept with gaps: three
# q6apm unmap fixes, the nt36536 Kconfig fix, the cpucp readq, seven UFS fixes; 0023 replaced by upstream
# 7cfdfdd65579). New: 0028-q91 (GPU, CPU boost, GENI, USB, robustness, audio and panel picks; runtime switches
# msm.a8xx_ab_vote / msm.gmu_hfi_irq_fix default off; Qualcomm's INT2 path only with an opt-in DTB), 0029-q91b
